WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.160
I've lived in this area my entire life.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.360
Right on the United States border.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.480
Just a half a mile
across the river from Detroit.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:13.920
I've been a scuba diver

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.280
and a diving instructor for over 25 years.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.840
I was a broke university student

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.360
and it was the only place I could dive.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.280
Because of wind and waves
the visibility is very limited, so

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.480
usually less than five feet and sometimes
as little as one foot of visibility.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.720
So when you can only see this far
in front of your face, it's going to limit

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.760
the people who are actually going
to want to do that dive.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.920
There is a very strong current
in the river

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:02.160
and it can really drag
you down the river quickly.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:07.160
It's an extremely dangerous 
environment, to say the least.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.400
I found that every single 
dive was an adventure.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.760
You could find bottles and cars and 
boats and shipwrecks and guns.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.160
And it just hooked me
and I’ve continued to do it

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.280
until this day.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.680
I was speaking with a local diver.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.520
He said he had found a vehicle
that was upside down,

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.720
laying in the middle of the Detroit River.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:39.880
And it was something that
definitely should not have been there.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.240
Since this was not something
that was well known.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.920
I wanted to follow up and see it
for myself.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:51.960
Now, remember,

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:55.240
with only a foot of visibility
in the river, it's easier said than done.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.960
I do a search pattern, so you just do a
zigzag on the bottom of the water.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:04.000
Just going back and forth
and just seeing what you can find.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.040
I actually saw it coming out of the gloom.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:13.840
Wooden spokes for a vehicle

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.440
that told me this
vehicle was very early.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:20.600
At that point,

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:24.000
I did not know anything
more about the history of it.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.160
I didn't know what kind of vehicle it was.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.680
But I really wanted to try and find out.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:34.720
I dove a couple of more times

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.720
and I used my underwater video 
camera with a high powered light

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:41.160
to really document
and get this evidence together.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.240
Just so I could try to build a model

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.440
of what I was seeing underwater.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.680
And what I saw was amazing.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.720
The vehicle was upside down.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.480
It was buried in the sediment.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:06.160
So all I could really see
was the bottom part

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.200
of the wheels.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.600
I could see the engine poking out,

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.960
but I really couldn't see anything
more of the top side of the vehicle.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:22.440
There was a wooden floorboard
and there was a truck bed.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:26.400
So very quickly, I determined that
this was not a car at all.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:27.680
It was actually a truck

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.400
lying close to the back was a heavy chain.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.000
We also saw a crank handle
on the front of the vehicle.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:40.480
You would actually have to crank
that motor to get it started.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:43.960
So the truck was old enough

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.040
not to have an electric starter motor,

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.320
but what kind of truck was it?

